{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/805168-give-me-some-clarification-breathe-deeply-snow-plague-garou-with-mnesis","id":805168,"title":"Give me some clarification: Breathe Deeply / Snow Plague / Garou with Mnesis?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T05:39:03-08:00","id":805168,"title":"Give me some clarification: Breathe Deeply / Snow Plague / Garou with Mnesis?","content":"Hello All,<br /> <br /> Please share me the your information about the book Breathe Deeply &amp; answer my questions below?<br /> <br /> First of all I have the Mokole Breedbook, which starts with a sort story of a werewolf, who, thank for the amazonian Mokole received Mnesis &amp; survived the Snow Plague.<br /> I would like to ask some guestions about this. (Unfortunatelly I haven't got the aforementioned novel &amp; live in a 2,5th world country where the Amazon don't want to send one.)<br /> <br /> 1) What is the Snow Palgue, where does it come from, what was the cure &amp; how is it associated with Mnetis &amp; the Pentex.<br /> 2) How could Peter receive Mnezis? Was it the Rite of Anamnesis, some other tool, or just the writer's all mighty power?<br /> 3) Did this received Mnesis act in any way other than written in the Breedbook?<br /> 4) Did anybody else received Mnezis?<br /> 5) Why did the prejudice consumed Mokole shared their greatest gift with a rat?<br /> <br /> Thank you for any of the answers in advance.<br /> <br /> W","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T11:37:46-08:00","id":805374,"title":"","content":"I read the novel a few years ago (it's sitting on my bookshelf), so I will answer what I remember:<br /> 1) The Snow Plague was a Pentex made spiritual disease that was connected to a cologne that Peter Ward was convinced to ware from a woman he was seeing (who turned out to be a Spiral). The cure ended up being a rare flower from the Amazon.<br /> 2) Peter received the mnesis more from what happened in the Mokole breed book then from Breath Deeply. From how I read it, it was more special snow flake &quot;DRAGON CHOSE YOU!&quot; then any cannon rite/gift that the Mokole have. <br /> 3) Not sure what you mean here, all of Peter's experience with the mnesis was pretty much shown in the breed book, not sure of any other material it may have popped in later. I don't remember him using any of it in Breath Deeply (like I said it came across to me as more of a chosen by Dragon snowflake moment then anything else)<br /> 4) No (though Nagah can get it with a 7 pt merit)<br /> 5) While the Mokole are described as angry and bitter, there is a lot of cannon material where they aren't really written that way (helping the Red Talons survive in Africa, the Bunyip in Australia, even meeting with Peter Ward in Australia for the breed book to happen, just to name a few). They help out in Breath Deeply though more because of the reputation the Ghost Raptors have built, and the fact that the Ghost Raptors follow the spirit of the Amazon as a totem. Peter was able to win over their trust so they spoke for him. But again it wasn't the Mokole who actually gave him the memory...but Dragon himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:17:27-08:00","id":805944,"title":"","content":"Thank you,<br /> <br /> This helped me but I came out with some additional questions if you don't mind:<br /> 1) What was the plague's effect?<br /> 2) How could this flower cure the plague?<br /> <br /> About my previous question:<br /> 3) You understood my question correctly.<br /> <br /> W","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:50:15-08:00","id":805961,"title":"","content":"It helps if you don't take special snowflakes as statements to what's actually normal in the setting. Be they Caine, The Perfect Metis or Samuel Haight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T04:28:27-08:00","id":805975,"title":"","content":"It can be kind of nice to use &quot;special snowflake&quot; elements in games. Especially if they are not that well known, like the plot of Breath Deeply.<br /> <br /> Iirc, the plague would have killed the entire sept, but the glaswalkers all entered into some kind of suspended animation. Peter was only a carrier for the plague, and he wasn't even infecting others as long as he used the cologne. The flower was a key component of the plague, iirc, so it could be used to create a anti-dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}